/target
# a worktree's own cargo target dirs, when one is used instead of the shared
# one (the views workspace is a separate workspace, and its wasm bundler is a
# third target). Rooted, so nothing named `target-*` deeper in the tree is
# swept by accident.
/target-views
/target-views-wasm
# labs is a standalone workspace (excluded from the root), so its build output
# lands outside the root-anchored /target above.
/crates/labs/target
/crates/views/target
# The Ice test runner writes per-test artifacts
# (screenshots + paint json) under the app crate's own target dir.
/app/target/
/.worktree/
# The guest kernel and rootfs ops/build-guest-rootfs.sh builds: ~900 MB of
# fetched-and-assembled artifacts, rebuilt from the script on any host.
/.guest/
# The macOS VMM shim's swiftc output (bin/duck-vz-shim/build.sh).
/bin/duck-vz-shim/.build/
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store
.claude/worktrees/
.codex/worktrees/
node_modules
# Brainstorm specs and implementation plans are per-PR working files, never a
# record: they stay local and die with their worktree.
docs/superpowers/
app/dist/
ops/wg-smoke/*.log
ops/wg-smoke/node*/

# superpowers SDD scratch
.superpowers/
package-lock.json

# Session handoff notes — local working state, never committed.
HANDOFF.md

# Key material a node or wallet writes (identity.key, user.key) never enters
# the tree, wherever a command was run from.
*.key

# wrangler local state (ops/auth-page)
.wrangler/

# graft's local graph cache — regenerable (`ops/graft build`), never committed
/graft/
